WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.670
Benzene is often drawn as a ring of six
carbon atoms, with three double bonds.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:10.730
Cyclohexene has just one double bond,
and bromine adds straight across it.

3
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.790
Benzene reacts with bromine
only when a catalyst is added,

4
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.770
and its product is not
the one cyclohexene gives.

5
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.190
Benzene is drawn with three double bonds.

6
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.710
So why doesn't it react like an alkene?

7
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:26.090
In this mission, you'll split
bonds into sigma and pi,

8
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:29.390
and match each atom to
its hybrid orbitals.

9
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.850
You'll find out what resonance
structures really mean,

10
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.210
and weigh up the evidence
on benzene's structure.

11
00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.470
Your mission: explain why benzene
doesn't behave like an alkene.
